I had some problems when my VS Code got stuck multiple times because agents were trying to run simple terminal commands, and my CPU flew to the moon. A reboot helped, of course. But I also suspected my `/bin/zsh` config — Oh My Zsh plus the Powerlevel10k theme — since it takes up to a second to load. I had no issues with `/bin/bash`. So I decided to check if I could keep my zsh shell for myself while telling agents to use bash instead.

Here's the fix for `settings.json`:

```json
"chat.tools.terminal.terminalProfile.osx": {
    "label": "bash",
    "path": "/bin/bash"
}
```

Might be useful for you too.
